contentText:
Happy You Seem Pretty Sad for a Girl So in Love Day! Olivia Rodrigo leads this week&#8217;s New Music Friday with her enthralling third studio album, led by the Billboard Hot 100 No. 1 hit &#8220;Drop Dead&#8221; and the top five hit &#8220;The Cure&#8221; (No. 5). Yet another emotional journey steered by the three-time Grammy winner and her longtime collaborator Dan Nigro, You Seem Pretty Sad finds Rodrigo delivering 13 gut-wrenching indie rock and pop-informed songs, this time bringing along The Cure&#8217;s Robert Smith for a standout track in &#8220;What&#8217;s Wrong With Me.&#8221;

