Bebe Rexha&#8217;s Dirty Blonde and Infinity Song&#8217;s new eponymous LP are also among the buzziest new full-length releases of the week. The former finds the &#8220;New Religion&#8221; singer offering her first album since partnering with EMPIRE, while the latter is the latest evolution from the Detroit-hailing, alt-rock family band. This New Music Friday also boasts new projects from Baauer ( U ), Blxst ( Labor of Love ), Jessie Reyez ( A Little Vengeance ), Hayley Kiyoko ( Girls Like Girls ), ANOTR ( Witness ) Keith Urban ( Flow State ), Myles Smith ( My Mess, My Heart, My Life ), Ruel ( Kicking My Feet & Screaming ), Spacey Jane ( Exit Wounds ), Cultura Profética ( En Bucle ), Sublime ( Until the Sun Explodes ) and Tori Kelly ( God Must Really Love Me ).

Over on the singles side, BTS leads the way with the arrival of &#8220;Come Over,&#8221; the group&#8217;s ARIRANG deluxe vinyl-exclusive bonus track, to streaming platforms. The song&#8217;s release is in celebration of the 13th anniversary of the group&#8217;s debut, and arrives during its annual Festa celebration. &#8220;This track was created with profound care and sincerity,&#8221; BigHit previously said of the track in a statement, adding that it &#8220;is a song that captures the sincere emotions of the artists as they prepare to reunite with fans after a long hiatus.&#8221;

On the other side of the musical spectrum, rocker Jack White shared &#8220;Dollar Bill,&#8221; the latest taste from his recently announced new album, due July 10. Jamaican dancehall star Ayetian, who emerged as the genre&#8217;s most nominated act at the 2026 Caribbean Music Awards, dropped a scathing new single titled &#8220;Chip,&#8221; and Grammy-winning North Carolina MC Rapsody linked up with the Karabo yaMorena Choir for &#8220;God Gotta Afro.&#8221;

This New Music Friday also offers new tracks from Nipsey Hussle (&#8220;Sacrifices&#8221;), Zacari (&#8220;Real Life&#8221;), Roy Woods (&#8220;Trust And Believe&#8221;), Tove Lo and Stromae (&#8220;Des Fleurs&#8221;), Ludacris and Glorilla (&#8220;Real Hustla&#8221;), Ayra Starr (&#8220;Tornado&#8221;), Aly & AJ (&#8220;Year of the Horse&#8221;), Fousheé (&#8220;Drive&#8221;), Chris Young and Breland (&#8220;If You&#8217;re Lucky&#8221;), Lauv (&#8220;Don&#8217;t You Know&#8221;), Warren Zeiders (&#8220;Days of My Life&#8221;), DJ GQ and Mr. Vegas (&#8220;If We Had More Time&#8221;), Kate Hudson (&#8220;California Dreamin'&#8221;), Toosii (&#8220;Yesterday&#8221;) and a collab among LE SSERAFIM, ILLIT and KATSEYE (&#8220;Iconic By Mistake&#8221;).

